WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.108
I've heard that great inventors dream up ideas in their sleep.

2
00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:11.612
I don't know if I dreamed my idea that night.

3
00:00:11.613 --> 00:00:16.799
But when I woke up early the next morning, I had the answer to Jenny's problem.

4
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.076
And the answer wasn't under my nose.

5
00:00:20.077 --> 00:00:24.415
It was on top of Jenny's nose!

6
00:00:24.416 --> 00:00:27.951
It was Saturday, so we didn't have school.

7
00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:32.704
I jumped out of bed and got dressed.

8
00:00:32.705 --> 00:00:38.334
Then I dashed downstairs, and knocked on Josh and Jenny's door.

9
00:00:38.335 --> 00:00:40.165
No one answered.

10
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:43.128
I knocked harder.

11
00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:48.991
Finally Mr. Chen came to the door, wearing his pajamas and bathrobe.

12
00:00:48.992 --> 00:00:51.544
Josh and Jenny stood behind him.

13
00:00:51.545 --> 00:00:57.669
"Jenny!" I cried. "I figured out why you're having trouble in school!"

14
00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:03.963
"Why?" asked Jenny, yawning and rubbing her eyes.

15
00:01:03.964 --> 00:01:07.415
"Because you can't see!" I said.

16
00:01:07.416 --> 00:01:10.953
"That's true," said Jenny.

17
00:01:10.954 --> 00:01:12.940
"You woke me up, Iggy!

18
00:01:12.941 --> 00:01:16.484
My eyes are still half-closed."

19
00:01:16.485 --> 00:01:20.792
"No!" I insisted. "That's not it.

20
00:01:20.793 --> 00:01:24.597
Remember when you tripped over the dog leash?"

21
00:01:24.598 --> 00:01:28.422
Jenny nodded. "I didn't even see it."

22
00:01:28.423 --> 00:01:33.081
"And you didn't want to call out numbers for the slide," I said.

23
00:01:33.082 --> 00:01:35.867
"Because you couldn't read them."

24
00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:38.499
Jenny blinked at me.

25
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.164
Mr. Chen was squinting too.

26
00:01:41.165 --> 00:01:43.366
He looked confused.

27
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.866
"I don't understand, Iggy.

28
00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:49.380
Jenny just got new glasses a few months ago."

29
00:01:49.381 --> 00:01:53.104
"And they work perfectly," said Jenny.

30
00:01:53.105 --> 00:01:57.605
"Yes, your glasses worked perfectly," I said.

31
00:01:57.606 --> 00:02:02.041
"But you haven't been wearing your glasses."

32
00:02:02.042 --> 00:02:05.205
"What do you mean?" asked Jenny.

33
00:02:05.206 --> 00:02:09.302
"Remember when you said you and Sara had the same glasses?"

34
00:02:09.303 --> 00:02:13.742
Jenny nodded. "Our glasses are the same color.

35
00:02:13.743 --> 00:02:16.514
But our eyes are very different.

36
00:02:16.515 --> 00:02:18.836
Sara can't see things close up.

37
00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:22.059
And I can't see things far away."

38
00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:29.134
"Right!" I said. "And you said Sara is having trouble in school now too."

39
00:02:29.135 --> 00:02:33.033
"Yes," said Jenny. "So?"

40
00:02:33.034 --> 00:02:38.059
"So your glasses probably got switched," I said.

41
00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:44.450
"I think you're wearing Sara's glasses and she's wearing yours!"

42
00:02:44.451 --> 00:02:48.079
By now Jenny's eyes were wide-open.

43
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.581
"I think you're right!" she said.

44
00:02:51.582 --> 00:02:55.211
"We were both crying when we said good-bye.

45
00:02:55.212 --> 00:02:58.296
So we had to take off our glasses.

46
00:02:58.297 --> 00:03:01.405
They must have gotten switched then."

47
00:03:01.406 --> 00:03:09.521
"Jenny," said Mr. Chen. "Can you go get your glasses?"

48
00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.155
Jenny got her glasses and put them on.

49
00:03:12.156 --> 00:03:15.829
Then Mr. Chen held up a newspaper.

50
00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.448
"Can you read this?"

51
00:03:17.449 --> 00:03:21.686
he asked, stepping back and pointing to a headline.

52
00:03:21.687 --> 00:03:24.141
Jenny peered at the newspaper.

53
00:03:24.142 --> 00:03:33.177
"No," she said. "The letters look blurry."

54
00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:36.879
"Then Iggy is right!" said Josh.

55
00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:41.522
Mr. Chen smiled. He looked relieved.

56
00:03:41.523 --> 00:03:43.287
"Iggy, that was amazing!

57
00:03:43.288 --> 00:03:46.922
You are a true problem-solver."

58
00:03:46.923 --> 00:03:49.554
"Thanks!" I said, grinning.

59
00:03:49.555 --> 00:03:54.047
"Let's have pancakes to celebrate," said Mr. Chen.

60
00:03:54.048 --> 00:04:01.641
"After breakfast I'll call Sara's mom and dad and tell them about what happened."

61
00:04:01.642 --> 00:04:06.612
That afternoon Jenny and Sara met and switched glasses.

62
00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:11.740
After that neither of them had any more problems in school.

63
00:04:11.741 --> 00:04:16.424
On Monday Mr. Bright, the inventor, came to our school.

64
00:04:16.425 --> 00:04:20.293
He showed us some of his latest inventions.

65
00:04:20.294 --> 00:04:24.337
One of them was a little umbrella for a dog.

66
00:04:24.338 --> 00:04:31.325
You could attach it to a dog's collar so the dog wouldn't get wet.

67
00:04:31.326 --> 00:04:39.870
Mr. Bright brought his dog onstage and showed us how it worked.

68
00:04:39.871 --> 00:04:44.401
All the kids loved it.

69
00:04:44.402 --> 00:04:49.680
"I know many of you are good inventors too," said Mr. Bright.

70
00:04:49.681 --> 00:04:52.712
It seemed like he was looking right at me.

71
00:04:52.713 --> 00:04:56.745
He probably loved my Pick-a-Number invention!

72
00:04:56.746 --> 00:05:01.746
"I have been reading your invention ideas," Mr. Bright went on.

73
00:05:01.747 --> 00:05:05.689
"And I've chosen one to be included in my new book."

74
00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:09.612
Mr. Bright took a piece of paper from his jacket pocket.

75
00:05:09.613 --> 00:05:16.509
I held my breath, waiting for him to call out my name.

